## Why This Is Asked
Real-world fintech ML requires low-latency scoring, robust drift handling, and strict auditing. The two-tier approach balances speed and accuracy, while feature stores and drift detectors address production reliability. The privacy angle forces region-aware controls and compliant data flows.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time inference with online/offline learning
- Streaming feature stores and windowing
- Calibration and drift detection
- Auditing and privacy/compliance constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: online score update using SGD
let w = initWeights();
for (event of stream) {
  let x = extractFeatures(event); // windowed features
  let p = sigmoid(dot(w, x));
  updateWeights(w, x, label, p);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency under peak load across regions?
- What drift-detection metrics would you track and how would you trigger retraining?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design an online, latency-constrained text classifier with limited features and simple drift checks, testing hashing-based features, SGD/partial_fit, and streaming evaluation.

## Key Concepts
- Hashing-based text features (30 features)
- Online learning with partial_fit
- Latency constraints on CPU
- Drift checks and calibration
- Evaluation metrics for spam detection (precision, recall, F1, PR-AUC)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple online logistic regression with partial_fit (conceptual)
class OnlineLR {
  constructor(nFeatures){ this.w = new Float64Array(nFeatures); this.b = 0; }
  predict(x){ let s=this.b; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) s+= this.w[i]*x[i]; return 1/(1+Math.exp(-s)); }
  partial_fit(x,y,lr=0.1){ const p=this.predict(x); const g=y-p; for(let i=0;i<x.length;i++) this.w[i]+=lr*g*x[i]; this.b+=lr*g; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for multiclass spam types (phishing, promo, etc.)?
- What changes if label latency increases from seconds to minutes?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design for real-time fraud scoring at scale with privacy constraints, multi-tenant data sharing, and safe rollbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming feature store and time-window features
- Hybrid inference paths: server-side and on-device
- Federated learning with differential privacy
- Drift detection and canary-based rollout strategies
- Model calibration and per-transaction explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo scoring sketch
function score(tx, globalModel, localModel){
  const feats = extract(tx)
  const s1 = globalModel.predict(feats)
  const s2 = localModel.predict(feats)
  return calibrate((0.6*s1 + 0.4*s2));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label latency for online updates?
- What metrics trigger rollback and how would you test rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-preserving ML at the edge, multi-modal fusion, and end-to-end latency budgeting across mobile and server.

## Key Concepts
- On-device ML, gated multi-modal fusion
- Federated learning, secure aggregation, DP
- Online drift detection, calibration, rollouts
- Data schema for cross-platform signals and privacy controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo forward for gated fusion
function forward(x1, x2, x3){
  const f1 = enc1(x1); const f2 = enc2(x2); const f3 = enc3(x3);
  const z = gate([f1,f2,f3]);
  return head(z);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency budgets in production?
- What privacy budgets would you set for DP in FL, and why?
